menu "Optical Flow Configuration"

    choice OPTFLOW_BOARD
        prompt "Camera board"
        default OPTFLOW_BOARD_AI_THINKER
        help
            Selects the pin map in camera_pins.h.

        config OPTFLOW_BOARD_AI_THINKER
            bool "AI-Thinker ESP32-CAM"
        config OPTFLOW_BOARD_ESP_EYE
            bool "ESP-EYE"
        config OPTFLOW_BOARD_XIAO_S3
            bool "Seeed XIAO ESP32S3 Sense"
    endchoice

    config OPTFLOW_TARGET_FPS
        int "Target frame rate (frames per second)"
        range 1 30
        default 15
        help
            Frames are paced to this rate deliberately. Optical flow for a blimp
            needs nothing faster, and running the sensor slower is the single
            most effective way to keep an ESP32-CAM cool. Changeable at runtime
            with the 'f' command.

    config OPTFLOW_XCLK_MHZ
        int "Sensor clock XCLK (MHz)"
        range 4 20
        default 10
        help
            The OV2640 pixel pipeline is clocked from this. 20 MHz is the usual
            example value; 10 MHz halves the sensor's own dissipation and is
            still far more bandwidth than a paced 15 FPS QQVGA stream needs.
            Below about 6 MHz some OV2640 modules fail to produce frames.

    config OPTFLOW_HEIGHT_MM
        int "Default height above the floor (mm)"
        range 100 10000
        default 2000
        help
            Used to convert pixel flow into millimetres per second. Pixel flow
            scales with 1/height, so this number must be right - or supplied by
            a rangefinder in flight. Changeable at runtime with the 'h' command.

    config OPTFLOW_HFOV_DEG
        int "Horizontal field of view (degrees)"
        range 10 150
        default 54
        help
            Horizontal FOV of the lens at the configured frame size. 54 degrees
            is the computed horizontal component of the stock OV2640 65-degree
            diagonal lens at 4:3. CALIBRATE THIS: it is a direct scale factor on
            every velocity this firmware reports.

    config OPTFLOW_BLOCK
        int "Match block size (pixels)"
        range 8 32
        default 16

    config OPTFLOW_SEARCH
        int "Search radius (pixels)"
        range 1 10
        default 7
        help
            Bounds the largest measurable motion: at QQVGA, 2 m height and
            15 FPS, 7 px is about +/-1.3 m/s. Larger costs cycles quadratically.

    config OPTFLOW_GRID
        int "Grid of match blocks (N x N)"
        range 1 8
        default 5
        help
            N*N blocks are matched per frame and the median is reported, so a
            person walking underneath cannot drag the estimate with them.

    config OPTFLOW_MIN_VAR
        int "Minimum block variance to attempt a match"
        range 0 10000
        default 50
        help
            A featureless floor patch has no recoverable motion. Blocks below
            this are reported as rejected rather than matched to noise.

endmenu
